# BharatWatch Cursor Rules

## Project Context
BharatWatch: self-healing local intelligence platform for Indian public data. Hackathon: WeMakeDevs × Bright Data, Aug 17–23, 2026.

## Code Style
- TypeScript: strict mode, functional components, explicit return types.
- React: Next.js App Router, server components by default, client components only when needed.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui base components.
- State: TanStack Query for server state, React useState for local UI state.

## File Structure
- `dashboard/app/page.tsx` — overview
- `dashboard/app/modules/<module>/page.tsx` — module view
- `dashboard/components/` — shared components
- `dashboard/lib/api.ts` — API client

## Conventions
- Use `cn()` helper from `class-variance-authority` + `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`.
- Components are PascalCase. Files are kebab-case.
- All API calls go through `lib/api.ts`.
- No secrets in code. Use env vars.

## Documentation
Update `docs/DESIGN.html` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.html` when UI or data flow changes.

## Demo First
Only build features that can be shown in a 5-minute demo video.
